## 5. Important Trade-offs

| Decision | Alternative Considered | Trade-off & Justification |
|---|---|---|
| **`setImmediate` background dispatch in Phase 3** | Synchronous execution | Synchronous execution would block HTTP connections for seconds. `setImmediate` provides non-blocking async execution inside Node.js now, perfectly matching the async contract that will transition to Redis/BullMQ in Phase 5. |
| **Fail-fast on first failing test case** | Run all test cases regardless | Running all test cases gives complete stats (e.g. "passed 8/10"), but consumes up to 10x more CPU/time on bad submissions. Fail-fast protects server compute while giving competitive programming-standard feedback. |
| **Per-testcase process spawn** | Long-running interactive process | Spawning a fresh process per test case resets process memory and state, preventing side effects between test cases (e.g. static variables or memory leaks). Trade-off: Small startup overhead per process, negligible for our time limits. |

